pcr-extended-locality: PCR reset and extend reject extended localities

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

Specification (TPM 2.0 Part 1, "Locality"): "Localities 0 through 4 are
represented as bits in the byte with 0000 0001 representing locality 0 and
0001 0000 representing locality 4. [...] A second representation is for
localities above 4. These are called *extended localities*. For extended
localities, the locality byte is an integer value representing the locality.
[...] The range of extended localities is 32-255."

PCRIsResetAllowed() and PCRIsExtendAllowed() compute the bit of the command
locality as `1 << locality` and test it against the PCR's reset/extend
locality bitmap (localities 0-4). For an extended locality the shift is
undefined behavior (on x86 it shifts by locality % 32), so e.g. locality 67
acts as locality 3 and locality 68 as locality 4, and PCRs restricted to those
localities can be extended or reset from an extended locality. An extended
locality is not a member of the bitmap; the patch rejects it (TPM_RC_LOCALITY),
as tpm-rs does. Found by differential fuzzing.
diff --git a/src/PCR.c b/src/PCR.c
--- a/src/PCR.c
+++ b/src/PCR.c
@@ -712,6 +712,11 @@
 
     // Check for the locality
     commandLocality = _plat__LocalityGet();
+    // tpm-rs differential testing -- C-ref spec deviation fix (NOT determinism):
+    // an extended locality (32-255) is an integer, not a bit of the PCR's
+    // locality bitmap (localities 0-4); shifting by it is undefined.
+    if(commandLocality > 4)
+        return FALSE;
 
 #ifdef DRTM_PCR
     // For a TPM that does DRTM, Reset is not allowed at locality 4
@@ -762,6 +767,11 @@
 
     // Check for the locality
     commandLocality = _plat__LocalityGet();
+    // tpm-rs differential testing -- C-ref spec deviation fix (NOT determinism):
+    // an extended locality (32-255) is an integer, not a bit of the PCR's
+    // locality bitmap (localities 0-4); shifting by it is undefined.
+    if(commandLocality > 4)
+        return FALSE;
     localityBits    = localityBits << commandLocality;
     if((localityBits & currentPcrAttributes.extendLocality) == 0)
 	return FALSE;
